{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For we shall not inherit, etc. For it has arrived, etc.</b> Its saying <b>for we shall not inherit</b> is the giving of a reason for what they said nearby: ״עַד הִתְנַחֵל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל</b> etc. — that they removed themselves from the inheritance. Therefore they stated the reason: that we ascribe the inheritance to Israel and not to ourselves, for the reason of ״כִּי לֹא נִנְחַל אִתָּם כִּי בָאָה״ etc. — meaning, for the reason that our inheritance has arrived, etc. Or they intended to say that after they accepted upon themselves everything stated, it shall now be known that the reason for their request was not out of fear of the wars of the peoples, as the suspicion in Moses' words implied, but rather for the reason that they have no inheritance in the land, for HaShem had already given them their inheritance across the Jordan eastward."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:38.640694406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}